Parts of QL4M65 are licensed under other Free-software licenses as described in the source code

QL4M65 / CoreQL:
-----------------------

  QL4M65 is a Sinclair QL core for the MEGA65, ported on top of the
  MiSTer2MEGA65 framework and built on the MiSTer-devel QL_MiSTer core.
  The MEGA65 port itself (this repository), including the MiSTer2MEGA65
  integration, the microdrive emulation, and all MEGA65-specific work,
  was done by Jose Daniel Fernandez Santos (dfsantos), with the
  assistance of Claude Code (Anthropic) as an AI pair-programming tool
  throughout the design, debugging and documentation work.

  QL4M65 is a port of MiSTer-devel's QL_MiSTer
      done by the MiSTer Development Team
      Original GitHub Repository: https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/QL_MiSTer
      Significant contributors:
      * the MiSTer-devel QL_MiSTer core team

  QL_MiSTer is itself based on decades of Sinclair QL emulation and
  reverse-engineering work by the wider Sinclair QL community, including
  the Minerva ROM (by Laurence Reeves / Tony Tebby and the Minerva team)
  and QDOS/related system software originally by Sinclair Research and
  Tony Tebby.

Other than that and my own work, QL4M65 uses:
------------------------------------------------------

  * MiSTer2MEGA65 by The MiSTer2MEGA65 Development Team
    https://github.com/sy2002/MiSTer2MEGA65

  * QNICE Co-Processor and System-on-a-Chip for file operations and on-screen-menu by The QNICE Development Team
    https://github.com/sy2002/QNICE-FPGA

  * Various MEGA65 drivers taken from the MEGA65 VHDL source by Paul Gardner-Stephen
    https://github.com/MEGA65/mega65-core

  * VGA Timing Generator, done by Scott Larson
    https://www.digikey.com/eewiki/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=15925278

  * VGA to HDMI converter IP core, done by Adam Barnes
    https://github.com/amb5l/tyto2

  * AVALON SCALER used for scaling to 720p for HDMI, done by temlib.org
    http://temlib.org/site/?page_id=10

  * HyperRAM controller, done by MJoergen
    https://mjoergen.github.io/HyperRAM/

  * Debouncer: I/O debouncing used for the joysticks, done by Scott Larson
    https://www.digikey.com/eewiki/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=4980758

  * Anikki-16x16 font, archived and provided by k80w
    https://github.com/k80w/consolefonts

  * PSF font to text file converter nafe-0.1 by Corvus Corax
    https://sourceforge.net/projects/nafe/

  * PSF font to C include file converter psftools-1.1.1 by John Elliott
    https://www.seasip.info/Unix/PSF/
